ARTICLES['create-gif-from-images']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-create-gif-from-images',title:'How to Create an Animated GIF From Images Free Online',date:'June 2026',read:'4 min',cat:'Converter Tools',excerpt:'Turn photos or screenshots into an animated GIF. How to choose frame delay and dimensions, keep the file small, avoid banding, and when video is better.',html:'<p>Animated GIFs are one of the most shared formats on the internet — used in social media, email marketing, presentations and chat. Creating one used to require video editing software. Now you can do it in your browser.</p>\n<a href="/#/t/gif-maker" class="tool-cta-link">Create GIF Free →</a>\n<h2>Best uses for animated GIFs</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Social media</strong>: Twitter/X and LinkedIn support GIFs natively in posts</li><li><strong>Email marketing</strong>: Animated GIFs play in most email clients (except Outlook 2013–2016)</li><li><strong>Presentations</strong>: Add motion to PowerPoint or Google Slides without embedding video</li><li><strong>UI/UX prototypes</strong>: Show micro-interactions and transitions to clients</li><li><strong>Product demos</strong>: Show before/after, step-by-step or feature highlights</li></ul>\n<h2>Optimising GIF file size</h2>\n<p>GIFs are large compared to video. A 5-second GIF can easily reach 5–10MB. To keep file size manageable:</p>\n<ul><li>Keep dimensions small — 480px wide is usually enough for web</li><li>Reduce frame rate — 10–15 fps looks smooth for most content</li><li>Limit the colour palette — GIFs support max 256 colours</li><li>Keep duration under 5 seconds for email use (some clients block longer GIFs)</li></ul>\n<h2>GIF vs WebP vs MP4 — when to use each</h2>\n<p><strong>GIF</strong>: Use when you need universal compatibility. Works everywhere, no autoplay issues.</p>\n<p><strong>Animated WebP</strong>: 40–70% smaller than GIF at the same quality. Use the <a href="/#/t/gif-to-webp">GIF to WebP converter</a> to convert after creating.</p>\n<p><strong>MP4 video</strong>: Best for long animations. HTML video with autoplay+loop+muted mimics GIF behaviour at 90% smaller file size.</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>How many frames do I need for a smooth GIF?</summary><p>At least 10 frames per second for smooth motion. For simple animations like logo reveals or icon transitions, even 5–8 frames can look smooth.</p></details>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>Why is my GIF so large?</summary><p>GIFs use an inefficient palette system. Limit colours, reduce dimensions and frame count. Or convert to WebP with the <a href="/#/t/gif-to-webp">GIF to WebP converter</a> for much smaller files.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['reduce-pdf-file-size']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-reduce-pdf-file-size',title:'How to Reduce PDF File Size Without Losing Quality',date:'June 2026',read:'4 min',cat:'PDF Tools',excerpt:'Find out why your PDF is large and fix the cause: photos, scans, fonts or pages. Which compression level to choose and why some files refuse to shrink.',html:'<p>A 50MB PDF that should be 2MB is one of the most common frustrations in office work. Email providers reject large attachments, clients struggle to open them, and web forms have size limits. Here is how to fix it.</p>\n<a href="/#/t/pdf-compressor" class="tool-cta-link">Compress PDF Free →</a>\n<h2>Why PDFs become large</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Embedded images</strong>: The biggest culprit. A PDF with high-resolution photos can easily exceed 50MB</li><li><strong>Embedded fonts</strong>: Some PDFs embed entire font files rather than just used characters</li><li><strong>Scan quality</strong>: Scanned documents at 600 DPI create enormous files</li><li><strong>Unoptimised export</strong>: Default export settings from Word, InDesign or Photoshop are often unnecessarily large</li></ul>\n<h2>How much can you compress a PDF?</h2>\n<p>Results vary significantly based on content. Image-heavy PDFs typically compress by 60–80%. Text-only PDFs may only compress 10–20% since text is already efficient. A 10MB brochure PDF commonly reduces to 2–3MB with no visible quality loss.</p>\n<h2>When NOT to compress</h2>\n<ul><li>Legal or archival documents where pixel-perfect quality is required</li><li>PDFs intended for professional printing (need full resolution images)</li><li>PDFs that will be further edited in Photoshop or Illustrator</li></ul>\n<h2>Other ways to reduce PDF size</h2>\n<p><strong>Remove unnecessary pages</strong>: Use the <a href="/#/t/pdf-page-remover">PDF Page Remover</a> to delete blank pages, cover pages or appendices before sharing.</p>\n<p><strong>Split the PDF</strong>: Use the <a href="/#/t/pdf-splitter">PDF Splitter</a> to send only the relevant section rather than the entire document.</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>What is the maximum PDF size for Gmail?</summary><p>Gmail allows attachments up to 25MB. For larger files, use Google Drive and share a link. Compress the PDF first with the <a href="/#/t/pdf-compressor">PDF Compressor</a> to stay under the limit.</p></details>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>Does compressing a PDF affect the text?</summary><p>No. Text compression is lossless — the text remains perfectly readable and searchable. Only image quality is affected when using lossy compression.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['create-qr-code-business']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-create-qr-code-business',title:'How to Create a QR Code for Your Business — Free Generator',date:'June 2026',read:'4 min',cat:'Converter Tools',excerpt:'Create a QR code that scans first time. The right size for the distance, quiet zone, colours, Wi-Fi and WhatsApp codes, and how to keep the link changeable.',html:'<p>QR codes have made a permanent comeback. Restaurant menus, business cards, product packaging, event posters — they appear everywhere. Generating one takes 10 seconds and costs nothing.</p>\n<a href="/#/t/qr-code-generator" class="tool-cta-link">Generate QR Code Free →</a>\n<h2>What can a QR code link to?</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Website URL</strong>: Direct visitors to your homepage or a specific landing page</li><li><strong>Google Maps</strong>: Link to your business location for easy navigation</li><li><strong>WhatsApp</strong>: Pre-fill a message to your business number</li><li><strong>PDF menu or brochure</strong>: Host on Google Drive and link to the share URL</li><li><strong>Social media profile</strong>: Instagram, LinkedIn, or any platform URL</li><li><strong>Payment link</strong>: UPI, PayPal, or Razorpay payment URLs</li><li><strong>Plain text</strong>: WiFi passwords, short instructions, contact information</li></ul>\n<h2>QR code size for print</h2>\n<p>Download at the highest resolution available. For print use:</p>\n<ul><li>Business card: minimum 2cm × 2cm (800px at 300 DPI)</li><li>A4 poster: minimum 4cm × 4cm</li><li>Outdoor banner: minimum 8cm × 8cm</li></ul>\n<p>Always test your printed QR code by scanning it before large print runs.</p>\n<h2>QR code best practices</h2>\n<ul><li>Always include a short URL hint below the QR code ("Scan to view menu")</li><li>Leave white space (quiet zone) around the code — do not crop edges</li><li>Test at the smallest size you plan to print it</li><li>Use a dark code on a white or light background (not the reverse)</li><li>For business use, use a URL shortener so you can change the destination without reprinting</li></ul>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>How long does a QR code last?</summary><p>Forever, if the URL it points to stays live. If the website goes down, the QR code stops working. Use a URL shortener (like bit.ly) so you can redirect the code even after printing.</p></details>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>Can I put a logo inside a QR code?</summary><p>QR codes have built-in error correction that allows up to 30% of the pattern to be obscured. A small logo in the centre works — but always test that it still scans reliably after adding the logo.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['best-free-tools-designers-2026']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-best-free-tools-designers-2026',title:'20 Best Free Online Tools for Graphic Designers in 2026',date:'June 2026',read:'3 min',cat:'Image Tools',excerpt:'Twenty free browser tools for graphic and web designers and freelancers, sorted by task, with honest limits and five workflows from logo to final delivery.',html:'<p>The best design tools used to cost hundreds of dollars per year. In 2026, a huge range of professional-grade tools run entirely free in your browser. Here are the most useful ones.</p>\n<h2>Image tools</h2>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/image-compressor">Image Compressor</a></h3>\n<p>Reduce image file sizes by up to 80% without visible quality loss. Essential before uploading anything to a website or sending by email.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/image-resizer">Image Resizer</a></h3>\n<p>Resize to exact pixel dimensions or percentage. Batch process multiple images at once.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/social-image-resizer">Social Media Image Resizer</a></h3>\n<p>Resize any image for Instagram, Facebook, Twitter/X, LinkedIn, YouTube, Pinterest and more — all with drag-to-crop.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/watermark-image">Watermark Tool</a></h3>\n<p>Add a text or image watermark to protect your work before sharing portfolio images or client previews.</p>\n<h2>Color tools</h2>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/color-palette-gen">Color Palette Generator</a></h3>\n<p>Extract a palette from any image OR generate complementary, analogous, and triadic palettes from a base colour. Get HEX, RGB, and HSL values.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/brand-color-extract">Brand Color Extractor</a></h3>\n<p>Upload a logo and extract the exact brand colours as CSS variables. Essential when starting a new client project.</p>\n<h2>PDF tools</h2>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/pdf-merger">PDF Merger</a></h3>\n<p>Combine multiple PDFs into one. Reorder files before merging. No file size limits.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/pdf-compressor">PDF Compressor</a></h3>\n<p>Compress large PDF presentations and brochures for email and web delivery.</p>\n<h2>Marketing design tools</h2>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/og-image-gen">OG Image Generator</a></h3>\n<p>Design 1200×630 Open Graph images for social media link previews. Text, brand colours, logo — download as PNG.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/cta-button-gen">CTA Button Generator</a></h3>\n<p>Design CTA buttons with live preview and copy the CSS directly. No Figma needed for simple button design tasks.</p>\n<div class="art-callout"><p>All tools on Tarumak Studio are 100% free, browser-based, and private. Your files never leave your device.</p></div>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>Are browser-based design tools as good as Photoshop?</summary><p>For specific tasks — compression, resizing, format conversion, colour extraction — yes. For complex compositing, illustration, or multi-layer editing, dedicated software still has advantages. The tools above replace Photoshop for probably 80% of everyday design tasks.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['add-watermark-photos']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-add-watermark-photos',title:'How to Add a Watermark to Photos Online — Protect Your Work',date:'June 2026',read:'4 min',cat:'Image Tools',excerpt:'Where to put a watermark, how strong to make it, when to tile it, and what it can and cannot protect. With settings for portfolios, proofs and product photos.',html:'<p>Sharing your work online without a watermark risks others using it without credit or payment. A professional watermark takes 30 seconds to add and protects every image you share.</p>\n<a href="/#/t/watermark-image" class="tool-cta-link">Add Watermark Free →</a>\n<h2>Text vs image watermarks — which to use?</h2>\n<p><strong>Text watermarks</strong> are ideal for most use cases. Include your name, website, or Instagram handle. Simple, fast, and universally readable.</p>\n<p><strong>Image watermarks</strong> (your logo) look more professional and reinforce branding. Use a PNG with a transparent background for the best result.</p>\n<h2>Watermark positioning tips</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Bottom-right corner</strong>: The most common position. Visible but not intrusive</li><li><strong>Centre at 10–20% opacity</strong>: Harder to crop out, but affects the viewing experience. Use only for high-value work you want to protect strongly</li><li><strong>Multiple watermarks</strong>: A grid of watermarks across the image is the most effective protection but least professional looking</li></ul>\n<h2>Opacity settings</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>30–40% opacity</strong>: Clearly visible, professional-looking</li><li><strong>15–25% opacity</strong>: Subtle, for presentation portfolios where you still want the image to look clean</li><li><strong>50–70% opacity</strong>: Maximum protection for high-value images shared in public galleries</li></ul>\n<h2>Before sharing client previews</h2>\n<p>Always watermark client work before sharing mockups or previews. Clients sometimes share previews internally before payment is complete. A watermark ensures work cannot be used without your permission.</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>Can watermarks be removed?</summary><p>A corner watermark can be cropped. A semi-transparent watermark covering the image is much harder to remove. For maximum protection, cover the central subject area of the image with a semi-transparent watermark.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['hashtag-strategy-instagram']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-hashtag-strategy-instagram',title:'Hashtag Strategy for Instagram and Twitter in 2026 — Free Generator',date:'June 2026',read:'4 min',cat:'Marketing Designer',excerpt:'What hashtags still do, how many to use on each network, how to research your own set in half an hour and how to find out whether they bring you anything.',html:'<p>Hashtags done right can put your posts in front of thousands of people who have never heard of you. Done wrong, they look like spam and get your account suppressed. Here is what actually works in 2026.</p>\n<h2>How many hashtags to use in 2026</h2>\n<p><strong>Instagram</strong>: 3–5 highly relevant hashtags outperform 30 generic ones. Instagram\'s own data shows posts with 3–5 targeted hashtags get better reach than those with 20+. The algorithm now prioritises content relevance over hashtag volume.</p>\n<p><strong>Twitter/X</strong>: 1–2 maximum. More than 2 hashtags on Twitter reduces engagement by up to 17% according to published studies.</p>\n<p><strong>LinkedIn</strong>: 3–5 professional, topic-specific hashtags. Avoid generic tags like #business or #success — too broad to drive quality engagement.</p>\n<h2>Three types of hashtags to mix</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Niche hashtags</strong> (5,000–100,000 posts): Best for reaching engaged audiences. #FreelanceDesigner, #UIUXDesign, #BrandIdentityDesign</li><li><strong>Medium hashtags</strong> (100,000–500,000 posts): Moderate competition, good visibility. #GraphicDesign, #WebDesign, #LogoDesign</li><li><strong>Broad hashtags</strong> (1M+ posts): High competition, limited value. Use sparingly as one of your 3–5</li></ul>\n<h2>How to research hashtags</h2>\n<ol><li>Search your main keyword on Instagram and check the "Related" section</li><li>Look at what hashtags your top competitors use on their best-performing posts</li><li>Check hashtag size — aim for niche and medium tags, not oversaturated ones</li><li>Rotate hashtag sets to avoid being flagged as repetitive</li></ol>\n<h2>Hashtags for designers</h2>\n<p>High-performing design hashtags: #UIDesign #UXDesign #BrandDesign #FreelanceDesigner #DesignerLife #GraphicDesigner #LogoDesigner #DigitalMarketing #CreativeDirection #DesignInspiration</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>Do hashtags still work in 2026?</summary><p>Yes, but the strategy has shifted. Fewer, more targeted hashtags now outperform large hashtag lists. Instagram\'s algorithm now uses semantic understanding of post content — hashtags supplement this but no longer drive it.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['meta-tags-seo-guide']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-meta-tags-seo-guide',title:'Meta Tags for SEO — Complete Guide with Examples (2026)',date:'June 2026',read:'4 min',cat:'Developer Tools',excerpt:'Title, description, canonical, robots and Open Graph tags explained with examples: what Google uses, what it ignores, and how to check your own pages.',html:'<p>Meta tags are the first thing Google and social media platforms read about your page. Getting them right can be the difference between ranking on page 1 and being invisible. This guide covers every tag that matters.</p>\n<h2>Title tag — the most important SEO element</h2>\n<p>The title tag appears in search results as the clickable blue headline. It is the single most important on-page SEO element.</p>\n<div class="art-callout"><p>&lt;title&gt;Free Image Compressor Online — Reduce Size Without Losing Quality | Tarumak Studio&lt;/title&gt;</p></div>\n<ul><li><strong>Length</strong>: 50–60 characters (Google truncates at ~580px width)</li><li><strong>Format</strong>: Primary keyword | Secondary keyword | Brand name</li><li>Put the primary keyword first — Google gives more weight to words near the start</li><li>Unique title for every page — never duplicate titles</li></ul>\n<h2>Meta description — controls your click-through rate</h2>\n<p>The meta description appears under the title in search results. It does not directly affect rankings but significantly affects click-through rate (CTR).</p>\n<div class="art-callout"><p>&lt;meta name="description" content="Compress JPG, PNG and WebP images online for free. Reduce file size by up to 80% without visible quality loss — all in your browser, no uploads required."&gt;</p></div>\n<ul><li><strong>Length</strong>: 120–160 characters</li><li>Include the primary keyword naturally</li><li>Write it as an ad — it should make people want to click</li><li>Include a benefit or unique selling point</li></ul>\n<h2>Open Graph tags — for social media sharing</h2>\n<p>OG tags control how your page looks when shared on Facebook, Twitter, LinkedIn and WhatsApp. Without them, social platforms guess — often badly.</p>\n<div class="art-callout"><p>&lt;meta property="og:title" content="Your Page Title"&gt;<br>&lt;meta property="og:description" content="Your description"&gt;<br>&lt;meta property="og:image" content="https://yoursite.com/og-image.png"&gt;<br>&lt;meta property="og:url" content="https://yoursite.com/page"&gt;</p></div>\n<p>Create your OG image (1200×630 px) using the free <a href="/#/t/og-image-gen">OG Image Generator</a>.</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>Does meta description affect rankings?</summary><p>Not directly. Google sometimes ignores your meta description and writes its own based on page content. But a well-written meta description improves CTR, which signals relevance and can indirectly improve rankings.</p></details>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>What is the canonical tag?</summary><p>&lt;link rel="canonical" href="..."&gt; tells Google which URL is the "original" version of a page. Use it when the same content appears at multiple URLs to prevent duplicate content issues.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['pdf-to-jpg-convert']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-pdf-to-jpg-convert',title:'How to Convert PDF to JPG Online — Free, Fast and Private',date:'June 2026',read:'3 min',cat:'PDF Tools',excerpt:'Save PDF pages as JPG images. What resolution you get, when PNG or text extraction is the better choice, and how to prepare pages for slides, posts and print.',html:'<p>Sometimes you need an image version of a PDF — for a presentation, social media post, email, or to share a single page with someone who cannot open PDFs. Converting PDF to JPG takes seconds.</p>\n<a href="/#/t/pdf-to-jpg" class="tool-cta-link">Convert PDF to JPG Free →</a>\n<h2>When you need PDF to JPG conversion</h2>\n<ul><li>Sharing a specific page from a report on social media</li><li>Inserting a PDF page into a PowerPoint or Google Slides presentation</li><li>Sending a single page from a contract or document by email or WhatsApp</li><li>Creating a preview image of a PDF brochure for a website</li><li>Editing a PDF page in an image editor</li></ul>\n<h2>Quality tips for PDF to JPG conversion</h2>\n<p>The quality of the output JPG depends on the PDF renderer. For best results:</p>\n<ul><li>Keep the original PDF at the highest quality (do not compress it before converting)</li><li>If the output looks blurry, the source PDF may have low-resolution images embedded in it — this cannot be improved by the converter</li><li>Text in the output JPG is rasterised (becomes pixels) — if you need editable text, use PDF to Text instead</li></ul>\n<h2>Alternative: PDF to PNG for transparency</h2>\n<p>If the PDF has a white background you want to make transparent (for example, a logo or diagram on a white page), convert to PNG instead. PNG supports transparency where JPG does not. Use the <a href="/#/t/pdf-to-jpg">PDF to JPG tool</a> which also outputs PNG format.</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>Can I convert a multi-page PDF to separate JPG images?</summary><p>Yes. The converter extracts each page as a separate JPG image. You can then download them all at once or individually.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['color-palette-brand-guide']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-color-palette-brand-guide',title:'How to Create a Brand Color Palette — Complete Guide for Designers',date:'June 2026',read:'4 min',cat:'Marketing Designer',excerpt:'Build a brand palette that works on screens and paper: choose a main colour, add neutrals and states, test contrast, and hand it over as CSS variables.',html:'<p>A brand color palette is the foundation of visual identity. The right colors make a brand instantly recognisable — think of Coca-Cola red or WhatsApp green. Here is how to build one professionally.</p>\n<a href="/#/t/color-palette-gen" class="tool-cta-link">Generate Color Palette Free →</a>\n<h2>How many colors does a brand palette need?</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Primary color</strong>: 1 color — your main brand color, used most frequently</li><li><strong>Secondary colors</strong>: 2–3 colors — support the primary in design compositions</li><li><strong>Neutral colors</strong>: 2–3 — grays, off-whites, blacks for text and backgrounds</li><li><strong>Accent color</strong>: 1 — a contrasting pop color for CTAs and highlights</li></ul>\n<h2>Color psychology for brands</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Blue</strong>: Trust, professionalism, technology — banks, SaaS, healthcare</li><li><strong>Green</strong>: Growth, nature, health, money — finance, wellness, sustainability</li><li><strong>Orange/Red</strong>: Energy, urgency, appetite — food, retail, CTAs</li><li><strong>Purple</strong>: Premium, creativity, wisdom — luxury, education, beauty</li><li><strong>Black</strong>: Sophistication, luxury, power — fashion, automotive, premium</li><li><strong>Yellow</strong>: Optimism, warmth, caution — consumer brands, children, warnings</li></ul>\n<h2>Extracting colors from a logo</h2>\n<p>Already have a logo? Upload it to the <a href="/#/t/brand-color-extract">Brand Color Extractor</a> to get the exact HEX, RGB, and HSL values of every color in the design. This is essential when onboarding a new client — you get their brand colors in seconds.</p>\n<h2>Generating harmonious color schemes</h2>\n<p>Start with your primary color and use color theory to generate a full palette:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Complementary</strong>: Opposite on the color wheel — high contrast, energetic</li><li><strong>Analogous</strong>: Adjacent colors — harmonious, cohesive, calming</li><li><strong>Triadic</strong>: Three equidistant colors — vibrant, diverse, balanced</li></ul>\n<p>Use the <a href="/#/t/color-palette-gen">Color Palette Generator</a> to visualise all these schemes from any base color.</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>How do I save brand colors as CSS variables?</summary><p>Use the <a href="/#/t/brand-color-extract">Brand Color Extractor</a> to extract colors and download them as CSS custom properties (--brand-primary, --brand-secondary etc.) ready to paste into your stylesheet.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['instagram-story-size-guide']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-instagram-story-size-guide',title:'Instagram Story Size 2026 — Dimensions, Templates and Best Practices',date:'June 2026',read:'4 min',cat:'Marketing Designer',excerpt:'The right size for Instagram Stories and Reels covers, where the interface covers your design, how to adapt landscape photos, and a checklist before posting.',html:'<p>Instagram Stories get 500 million daily viewers. Getting the dimensions right means your content fills the screen beautifully instead of showing awkward white bars or cropped edges.</p>\n<a href="/#/t/social-image-resizer" class="tool-cta-link">Resize for Instagram Story Free →</a>\n<h2>Instagram Story dimensions 2026</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Size</strong>: 1080 × 1920 pixels (9:16 aspect ratio)</li><li><strong>File format</strong>: JPG or PNG for images, MP4 or MOV for video</li><li><strong>Maximum file size</strong>: 30MB for images, 4GB for video</li><li><strong>Safe zone</strong>: Keep important content in the central 1080 × 1420 px area to avoid being covered by UI elements</li></ul>\n<h2>Understanding the safe zone</h2>\n<p>Instagram overlays UI on top and bottom of Stories:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Top 250px</strong>: Username, profile photo, close button overlay — keep this area clear</li><li><strong>Bottom 250px</strong>: "Send message" bar and swipe-up area — keep this area clear</li><li><strong>Safe zone</strong>: The central 1080 × 1420 px region — place all key text and visuals here</li></ul>\n<h2>Story design best practices</h2>\n<ul><li>Use large, bold text — Stories are viewed on mobile screens at arm\'s length</li><li>Keep text in the safe zone, away from the top and bottom 250px</li><li>Use high-contrast colors — white text on dark background or dark text on light background</li><li>Include a clear CTA — "Swipe Up", "Link in Bio", "DM for details"</li><li>First 1–2 seconds determine if viewers watch the whole Story — make them count</li></ul>\n<h2>Instagram Reels cover image</h2>\n<p>Reels use the same 1080 × 1920 px format. The cover image (thumbnail) is cropped to 1080 × 1350 px when shown in the grid. Design your cover with this in mind.</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>Can I use a landscape image in an Instagram Story?</summary><p>Yes, but it will show with black bars above and below on most phones. Instagram sometimes auto-adds a blurred version of the image as a background fill. For best results, always use 9:16 format.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['best-free-marketing-tools']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-best-free-marketing-tools',title:'Best Free Marketing Tools for Designers and Creators in 2026',date:'June 2026',read:'3 min',cat:'Marketing Designer',excerpt:'Eight free browser tools for campaigns, from link previews and tracked links to lead magnets, with what each does well, its limits and three campaign plans.',html:'<p>Marketing tools used to mean expensive subscriptions. In 2026, every tool a designer or marketer needs for campaigns, social media, and content creation runs free in the browser. Here are the most useful ones.</p>\n<h2>Social media image tools</h2>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/social-image-resizer">Social Media Image Resizer</a></h3>\n<p>Resize any image to exact platform dimensions for Instagram, Facebook, Twitter/X, LinkedIn, YouTube, Pinterest and WhatsApp. Drag-to-crop, multiple modes. The single most-used marketing tool for any designer.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/og-image-gen">Open Graph Image Generator</a></h3>\n<p>Create 1200×630 OG images for link previews on social media. Add title text, brand colours and a logo — download as PNG. Essential for content marketers and bloggers.</p>\n<h2>Campaign and analytics tools</h2>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/utm-builder">UTM Link Builder</a></h3>\n<p>Build UTM-tagged campaign URLs for Google Analytics 4. Also decodes existing UTM links. Absolutely essential for tracking what actually drives website traffic.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/ad-copy-gen">Ad Copy Generator</a></h3>\n<p>Generate headlines, body copy and CTAs for Facebook, Google and Instagram ads. Template-based — no AI subscription needed.</p>\n<h2>Brand and design tools</h2>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/color-palette-gen">Color Palette Generator</a></h3>\n<p>Extract color palettes from images or generate harmonious color schemes. Ideal for maintaining brand consistency across campaigns.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/brand-color-extract">Brand Color Extractor</a></h3>\n<p>Upload a client\'s logo and extract the exact brand colors as HEX, RGB, HSL and CSS variables in seconds.</p>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/cta-button-gen">CTA Button Generator</a></h3>\n<p>Design call-to-action buttons with live preview and download as PNG or copy the CSS. Great for landing page prototypes and client presentations.</p>\n<h2>Lead generation tools</h2>\n<h3><a href="/#/t/pdf-lead-magnet">PDF Lead Magnet Creator</a></h3>\n<p>Build professional PDF checklists, guides and cheatsheets to grow an email list. Choose template style, add brand colours, download instantly.</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>What is the most important free marketing tool?</summary><p>For most marketing designers, the Social Media Image Resizer and UTM Builder provide the most daily value. Image resizing is needed for every campaign; UTM tracking shows what actually works.</p></details>'};
ARTICLES['convert-jpg-to-pdf']={url:'https://tarumakstudio.com/article-convert-jpg-to-pdf',title:'How to Convert JPG to PDF Online — Free and Instant',date:'June 2026',read:'4 min',cat:'PDF Tools',excerpt:'Turn one or many JPG photos into a PDF. Which page size to choose, how to keep the file small enough for e-mail, and how to make phone scans look tidy.',html:'<p>Converting JPG images to PDF is one of the most common document tasks — for scanned documents, photo portfolios, or turning screenshots into a shareable PDF. No software required.</p>\n<a href="/#/t/jpg-to-pdf" class="tool-cta-link">Convert JPG to PDF Free →</a>\n<h2>Common reasons to convert JPG to PDF</h2>\n<ul><li>Combining multiple scanned document pages into one PDF</li><li>Creating a PDF portfolio from JPEG images</li><li>Converting screenshots into a shareable PDF report</li><li>Sending photos as a professional document (not a raw image file)</li><li>Combining before-and-after design images for client presentation</li></ul>\n<h2>How to combine multiple JPGs into one PDF</h2>\n<ol><li>Open the <a href="/#/t/jpg-to-pdf">JPG to PDF converter</a></li><li>Upload multiple JPG images at once</li><li>Drag to reorder if needed</li><li>Click "Convert to PDF"</li><li>Download the single PDF containing all images</li></ol>\n<h2>Image quality in the PDF</h2>\n<p>The converter maintains the original quality of your JPG images inside the PDF. The output quality equals the input quality — if your source image is sharp, the PDF will be sharp.</p>\n<h2>Related: images to PDF from multiple formats</h2>\n<p>If you have a mix of JPG, PNG, and WebP images, use the <a href="/#/t/images-to-pdf">Images to PDF tool</a> which accepts all common image formats in a single conversion.</p>\n<details class="art-faq"><summary>What is the maximum image size for JPG to PDF conversion?</summary><p>There is no artificial file size limit. The practical limit depends on your browser and available memory. For very large images (50MB+), processing may take a few seconds longer.</p></details>'};
